  "body": "**Blocked by:** #168, #84, #85\n\n## Context\n\nThis issue builds on #168; #170 is the next sequential slice of the `observability` batch.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd `observability_checks` with UUID id, unique check_key, ok/alerting status, detail, and changed_at. Register `observability.checkSystem` every minute. Check expected process beats; graphile backlog entering at pending >100 or oldest overdue >10 minutes and recovering below half; adapter-owned mail `next_expected_activity_at`; mail last_error; and permanent jobs. Persist transitions. Notify only on ok-to-alerting using process_stale, queue_backlog, or mail_sync_stalled, source_table observability_checks/source_id row UUID, targeting the single v1 user through canonical fanout.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Task deliverables, migrations, integration, automated tests, and necessary documentation.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- No LLM system checks or new channel.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Sustained faults notify once across restarts.\n- Recovery rearms a later notification.\n- Queue hysteresis prevents oscillation.\n- Notifications reference their check rows.\n- Provider-specific mail deadlines feed one predicate.\n",
